# Handoff Protocol — {{ project_name }}

The handoff contract is the **only** thing carried across an agent boundary. No stored
state machine. No separate log. The live artifacts plus this contract are the complete
state of the pipeline.

## Contract Schema

Every sub-agent receives and produces a JSON object with these fields:

```json
{
  "ticket_key":      "string  — REQUIRED. The tracker ticket identifier (e.g. PROJ-1234).",
  "td_doc_id":       "string  — OPTIONAL. ID or path of the TD doc. Required by: bdd-agent, manual-agent, automation-agent.",
  "test_section_id": "string  — OPTIONAL. Section/folder ID in {{ test_repo_label }}. Required by: manual-agent, automation-agent.",
  "test_case_ids":   ["array  — OPTIONAL. Case IDs from {{ test_repo_label }}. Required by: manual-agent, automation-agent."],
  "test_run_id":     "string  — OPTIONAL. Run/cycle ID in {{ test_repo_label }}. Required by: automation-agent.",
  "actions_taken":   ["array  — REQUIRED. Every action the agent performed, in order."],
  "routing": {
    "target": "string — bdd | manual | automation | test_design | done | done_simple"
  },
  "writeback_targets": ["array — Paths of .md reference files the main agent must update after receiving this contract."]
}
```

## Validation Rules

**The main agent runs these checks after every sub-agent returns:**

1. `ticket_key` is present and non-empty.
2. `actions_taken` is a non-empty array.
3. `routing.target` is one of the allowed values.
4. If `routing.target` is `bdd`, then `td_doc_id` is present.
5. If `routing.target` is `manual`, then `td_doc_id` and `test_case_ids` are present.
6. If `routing.target` is `automation`, then `test_case_ids` and `test_run_id` are present.
7. All `writeback_targets` listed have been written to by the agent.

**If any check fails:** re-dispatch the same agent with the violation list attached.

## Write-back Procedure

After a sub-agent returns a contract with `writeback_targets`, the **main agent** (not the
sub-agent) performs the write-back:

| Sub-agent | When to write back | Target file |
|---|---|---|
| bdd-agent | After publishing cases | `.claude/references/test-sections.md` |
| automation-agent | After writing the ledger | `.claude/references/automation-coverage.md` |

Write-back keeps the local reference cache current so that the next cold-start session
does not need a live {{ test_repo_label }} query to reconstruct state.

## Routing Decision Map

| `routing.target` | Means | Main agent action |
|---|---|---|
| `test_design` | TD doc missing, ACs unclear, or `failed_requirement` from manual | Spawn test-design-agent |
| `bdd` | TD at In Review (or Approved but no cases) | Spawn bdd-agent |
| `manual` | Cases published, no run yet | Spawn manual-agent |
| `automation` | All cases have verdicts, ≥1 automatable has no spec | Spawn automation-agent |
| `done` | All automatable cases automated, rest excluded | Run final compliance pass |
| `done_simple` | Simple feature path — QA brief published, no test repo needed | Done (no further agents) |

## Escalation

If the same phase has been re-dispatched **3 times** without resolving the violation:
- Stop dispatching.
{% if has_comm_platform %}
- Post a human-escalation message to {{ comm_platform_label }} `{{ comm_platform_channel }}`.
{% endif %}
- Include the violation list and the three `actions_taken` logs in the escalation.
- Halt — do not attempt a fourth dispatch.
